{"question_id": "V2-dev-LAW-en-T2-001", "approach": "B1", "approach_base": "B1", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "L", "corpus_set": "LAW_en", "answer_text": "Yes, the Act reaches this conduct, under section 6 (bribery of a foreign public official).\n\n- Section 6(1) makes it an offence where a person bribes a foreign public official with the intention of influencing them in that capacity; a French ministry official holds an administrative position of a country outside the UK, so qualifies as a foreign public official under section 6(4)(a).\n- Section 6(2) with (2)(a) requires that P also intends to obtain or retain business, which is satisfied by seeking to win the government contract.\n- Although no act or omission forming part of the offence takes place in the UK (section 12(2)(a)), the offence still applies because the person has a close connection with the UK (section 12(2)(c)).\n- Under section 12(4), a person has such a close connection if, at the relevant time, they were a British citizen (section 12(4)(a)).", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 166 chars]", "doc_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en", "section_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::o010", "unit_ids": ["L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b67"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 0, "span": [6284, 6450], "meta": {}}, {"text": "[stripped: 43 chars]", "doc_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en", "section_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::o010", "unit_ids": ["L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b68"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 1, "span": [6452, 6495], "meta": {}}, {"text": "[stripped: 16 chars]", "doc_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en", "section_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::o010", "unit_ids": ["L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b69"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 2, "span": [6497, 6513], "meta": {}}, {"text": "[stripped: 209 chars]", "doc_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en", "section_id":