{"question_id": "V2-dev-LAW-en-T3-001", "approach": "B1", "approach_base": "B1", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "L", "corpus_set": "LAW_en", "answer_text": "Data Governance Act - natural person: Yes, but only a natural person who is not a data subject with respect to the specific data in question.\nData Governance Act - basis: The right to grant access to or to share certain personal data or non-personal data, in accordance with applicable Union or national law.\nData Act - natural person: Yes, a natural or legal person can be a data holder.\nData Act - basis: The right or obligation to use and make available data, in accordance with the Data Act, applicable Union law or national legislation adopted in accordance with Union law.\n\nBoth allow natural persons to be data holders, but the Data Governance Act excludes data subjects with respect to the specific data, while the Data Act does not. The status is based on the right to grant access to or share data under the Data Governance Act, versus the right or obligation to use and make available data under the Data Act.", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 345 chars]", "doc_id": "L.eurlex-32022R0868_data-governance-act.en", "section_id": "L.eurlex-32022R0868_data-governance-act.en::o007", "unit_ids": ["L.eurlex-32022R0868_data-governance-act.en::p1_b102"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 0, "span": [84937, 85282], "meta": {}}, {"text": "[stripped: 390 chars]", "doc_id": "L.eurlex-32023R2854_data-act.en", "section_id": "L.eurlex-32023R2854_data-act.en::o007", "unit_ids": ["L.eurlex-32023R2854_data-act.en::p1_b181"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 1, "span": [152785, 153175], "meta": {}}], "evidence_units": ["L.eurlex-32022R0868_data-governance-act.en::p1_b102", "L.eurlex-32023R2854_data-act.en::p1_b181"], "evidence_items": [{"doc_id": "L.eurlex-32022R0868_data-governance-act.en", "section_id": "L.eurlex-32022R0868_data-governance-act.en: