{"question_id": "V2-dev-LAW-en-T3-002", "approach": "B1", "approach_base": "B1", "flags": {}, "setting": "en-en", "q_lang": "en", "d_lang": "en", "corpus": "L", "corpus_set": "LAW_en", "answer_text": "Bribery Act 2010, section 7 - version 2010 CHAPTER 23: a relevant commercial organisation is guilty of an offence if a person associated with it bribes another person intending (evidence [1]); a person guilty of an offence under section 7 is liable on conviction on indictment to a fine (evidence [2]).\nModern Slavery Act 2015, section 54 - version 2015 CHAPTER 30: a commercial organisation must prepare a slavery and human trafficking statement for each financial year (evidence [4]); the duties are enforceable by the Secretary of State bringing civil proceedings in the High Court for an injunction or, in Scotland, for specific performance of a statutory duty under section 45 of the Court of Session Act 1988 (evidence [5]).\n\nFailure to prevent bribery under the Bribery Act 2010 is a criminal offence, punishable by a fine on conviction on indictment. Failure to produce a slavery and human trafficking statement under the Modern Slavery Act 2015 is not a criminal offence; it is enforced through civil proceedings (injunction or specific performance) brought by the Secretary of State.", "abstained": false, "retrieved_units": [{"text": "[stripped: 156 chars]", "doc_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en", "section_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::o012", "unit_ids": ["L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b99"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 0, "span": [9154, 9310], "meta": {}}, {"text": "[stripped: 98 chars]", "doc_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en", "section_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::o017", "unit_ids": ["L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::p1_b155"], "kind": "unit", "score": null, "rank": 1, "span": [16249, 16347], "meta": {}}, {"text": "[stripped: 155 chars]", "doc_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en", "section_id": "L.ukpga-2010-23_bribery-act.en::o01